<title>FRANCE: Bertrand Faure sells Portugal unit.</title>
<headline>Bertrand Faure sells Portugal unit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>French car seat maker Bertrand Faure said on Tuesday it has signed an agreement to sell its Flexipol Portuguese subsidiary to Copo of Spain.</p>
<p>Flexipol makes foam blocks. The sale is part of Bertrand Faure's aim of focusing on its core passenger seat business, the company said in a statement. No sale price was given.</p>
<p>In the second half 1996, Bertrand Faure has sold KSTW of Germany, which makes plastic parts and garden furniture, and NCS of France, which makes fireworks and airbag release mechanisms.</p>
<p>The sales will help reduce group debt by about 100 million francs.</p>
